WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.164 --> 00:00:10.882
In tutorial 9.4, you'll connect the
mailbox your pitches go out from.

00:00:11.912 --> 00:00:15.637
First, open Company settings,
then the Mailboxes tab.

00:00:15.687 --> 00:00:17.846
This is where your
pitches get their sender.

00:00:18.841 --> 00:00:23.491
With Microsoft 365 or Gmail,
connect without a password.

00:00:23.541 --> 00:00:29.411
Click Connect Microsoft 365 or
Connect Gmail, sign in, and allow it.

00:00:29.461 --> 00:00:31.039
No password is stored.

00:00:32.037 --> 00:00:35.397
Using another mail host,
like Zoho or Fastmail?

00:00:35.447 --> 00:00:38.266
Click Connect a mailbox,
and choose your provider.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:44.115
Then type your name and e-mail, and use
an app password, not your normal one.

00:00:44.165 --> 00:00:46.102
Show me how explains how to get it.

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:49.871
The rest of the form
matches the next steps.

00:00:49.921 --> 00:00:54.055
Then click Test and connect, and it
checks your mailbox before saving.

00:00:55.039 --> 00:00:58.014
Once it's connected, the
card shows your mailbox,

00:00:58.064 --> 00:01:01.497
today's e-mails against your
limits, and the hours it sends.

00:01:02.541 --> 00:01:06.521
Next, click Change on the card.
Add your name, your job title,

00:01:06.571 --> 00:01:09.867
and your business postal
address. The law asks for it.

00:01:11.016 --> 00:01:15.627
Now set your time zone, and the hours
pitches may go out, Monday to Friday.

00:01:17.491 --> 00:01:22.811
Then set first e-mails a day, up
to 30, and all e-mails, up to 50.

00:01:22.811 --> 00:01:25.440
A new mailbox warms up slowly on its own.

00:01:26.399 --> 00:01:30.789
Click Save. Then open Connection and
signature to check every setting.

00:01:30.839 --> 00:01:34.287
You can test the mailbox,
change it, or pause sending.

00:01:35.306 --> 00:01:40.306
Now pick the mailbox for this website.
Open Link building, and in Settings,

00:01:40.356 --> 00:01:43.373
Send from chooses the address
your pitches go out from.

00:01:44.342 --> 00:01:47.937
Pick an address on another domain,
and Check this first warns you:

00:01:47.987 --> 00:01:52.628
people are less likely to answer it.
Click Cancel, and keep your own address.

00:01:53.651 --> 00:01:58.804
Last, the Opt-out list on the Mailboxes
tab holds addresses and domains that never

00:01:58.804 --> 00:02:01.223
get another e-mail from your company.

00:02:02.198 --> 00:02:06.158
Type an address or a domain,
choose the kind, and click Add.

00:02:06.208 --> 00:02:09.375
People who say no, and
bounces, are added for you.

00:02:10.409 --> 00:02:13.684
Now your pitches go out from
your own address, a few a day,

00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:16.040
and replies come back to your inbox.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:20.705
If an inbox check is
missing, click Fix these.

00:02:20.755 --> 00:02:23.936
It walks you through the records
that keep your e-mails out of spam.

00:02:24.941 --> 00:02:30.216
So, to recap, connect your mailbox, add
your signature and address, set your limits,

00:02:30.266 --> 00:02:33.285
send from your own domain,
and keep your opt-out list.

00:02:34.309 --> 00:02:39.169
Next, review and approve link-building
pitches, in tutorial 9.5.
